<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
	<!--
		Hotspot Configuration: required by WiFiJoiner to call
		NEHotspotConfiguration and join the FlashAir card's WiFi network.

		This is an *unmanaged* entitlement: tick Hotspot on the App ID
		(Certificates → Identifiers → us.v9n.flashair-sync → Capabilities)
		and it is yours immediately. No request form, no Apple review — that
		is NEHotspotHelper, a different, managed entitlement this app does
		not use. Earlier versions of this comment said otherwise; they were
		wrong.

		What does bite: the capability has to be enabled on the App ID
		*before* the distribution provisioning profile is generated, or the
		archive fails with "Provisioning profile … doesn't support the
		Hotspot Configuration capability". Simulator builds don't care.
	-->
	<key>com.apple.developer.networking.HotspotConfiguration</key>
	<true/>
</dict>
</plist>
